All five asks are done, verified end to end, and the faculty roster is live in Supabase.

## Review of FacultyList.xlsx

204 rows under a header on row 2 (`S. No. | Name of the Faculty | MAHE ID | Department`), covering 5 departments (SOCE, SOEE, School of Basic Sciences Humanities & Management, Director MIT-BLR, Joint Director MIT-BLR). Two data problems worth knowing about:

- **Row 199, Dr. Nithish Kumar R has no MAHE ID.** There is nothing to search on, so it is the one row *not* in the database — see the skipped row in the seeder output. Fix it in the spreadsheet and re-run the seeder.
- **`MAHE0028678` is used by two people** (Dr. Akshatha Y and Dr. S Priya). I kept both rows rather than silently dropping one; searching that ID shows both and the name disambiguates. Same ID on the wrong person is worth fixing at the source.

## 1. Faculty data in the database

[006_faculty_directory.sql](supabase/migrations/006_faculty_directory.sql) adds `public.faculty`, and [scripts/seed-faculty.mjs](scripts/seed-faculty.mjs) loads the spreadsheet (run via `npm run db:seed-faculty`, or with a path argument). It upserts on `(mahe_id, name)`, so re-running corrects departments instead of duplicating people, and it prints skipped rows and shared IDs. I already applied it to your Supabase: **203 rows across 5 departments**, verified by querying the live table.

## 2–3. Search a MAHE ID, everything else fills in locked

[GET /api/faculty?q=](app/api/faculty/route.ts) searches the directory — ID-only, from 4 characters up, 10 results, rate-limited, so the roster can't be dumped. On [/attend/<id>](components/AttendForm.tsx) the only input is **Your MAHE ID**: type a full ID, a fragment (`23571`), or paste one with a space and it still matches; pick yourself from the results and the form switches to a read-only **Your details** panel (MAHE ID, name, department) with a "Not you? Change" link. There are no name or department fields at all now, and the submit button stays disabled until something is picked. The server re-reads the roster row when marking, so even a hand-crafted request can't store a conflicting name — I verified that with a deliberately wrong name and department.

## 4. Reporting a missing or wrong ID

"Can't find your MAHE ID?" / "These details aren't right?" opens a small form (reason + optional note, 500 chars) posting to [POST /api/faculty/reports](app/api/faculty/reports/route.ts). Reports land in `faculty_reports`, appear on the host page within about a second as **Directory reports** with the typed ID, the roster's own details, the reason and the note, and the host clears each one with **Resolve** ([AttendanceLive.tsx](components/AttendanceLive.tsx)).

One consequence worth deciding on later: a MAHE ID is now **required** to mark attendance, so anyone missing from the directory can only mark after the host adds them (or approves a join request). That follows from your "locked fields" requirement, but it is a real behavior change from the old optional college-ID field.

## What we use Supabase for

**Postgres** (transaction pooler via `postgres`, [lib/db.ts](lib/db.ts)) stores everything: `meetings` (title, host token, schedule, geofence, owning host), `attendance` (the mark, with `college_id` = the MAHE ID, department, device, GPS, distance), `join_requests` (geofence failures awaiting a decision), `hosts` + `host_sessions` (scrypt passphrase hashes, session-token hashes), and now `faculty` + `faculty_reports`. Unique indexes enforce one mark per person and per device and one pending request per device; `on delete cascade` from `meetings` removes attendance, requests and reports with it; RLS is on with no policies, so only the server's owner connection reaches these tables.

**Realtime** carries invalidation only: every write (a mark, a request, a decision, a resolve, an open/close) broadcasts a content-free `{ kind }` to that meeting's channel, and the host page answers by refetching its host-key-protected snapshot. With no publishable key it polls every 3 s instead — which is the state of this machine.

**Not used:** Supabase Auth (hosts have their own cookie sessions), Storage, Edge Functions, and `supabase-js` beyond the Realtime socket. This is now written up in the README under "What Supabase does here".

## Verification

43 unit tests pass (9 new for directory lookup and MAHE-ID normalisation, plus schema tests for the required ID and the report payload), `tsc --noEmit` clean, ESLint clean, `npm run build` succeeds, and a 30-check live API run against the dev server passed — search hit/miss/short-query, shared ID, identity override, report lifecycle including 403s without the host key and 404 on double-resolve, and both exports (the Excel report now reconciles present/absent against Postgres, 16 KB with the roster). In a real browser on the production build I typed a fragment, picked the match, saw the locked details, sent a report, watched it appear on the host page and resolve, then marked attendance and got the success card. Test meetings, attendance rows and reports were deleted afterwards; your 13 real meetings and 1 pre-existing attendance row are untouched.

Two things to note about this machine: I stopped my dev server and left the **production build preview running on http://localhost:3112** (registered in the Preview tab) because the dev server's HMR websocket in this browser panel sends both the home page and the attend page into a reload loop — it is not related to these changes, and `npm run dev` in your own browser is the normal path. Also, `.gitignore` now has a root-anchored `/*.xlsx` (plus `~$*` for Excel lock files) rather than a bare `*.xlsx`, because `app/api/meetings/[id]/export.xlsx/` is a route *directory* that a bare pattern would have swallowed.

Since a wrong department currently means editing the spreadsheet and re-seeding, the obvious next step is letting a host fix the directory from the page they already have open.
